# The octoflow-gate release (https://github.com/DavidSiegl/octoflow-gate/releases) that judges this repository's
# changes, as ci/fetch-gate.sh reads it: one line, the release's version and the sha256 of its
# octoflow-gate-<version>.tar.gz, as the release's .sha256 asset gives it. A build reads this file from its own tree
# (the Jenkinsfile's Gate stage). Raise it to a new release only after that release exists and its downloaded tarball
# has passed `sha256sum -c`; lower it to roll back to an earlier one, 0.7.0 or later: the Gate stage runs a release's
# `gate`, which the ones before do not ship, so going below 0.7.0 means reverting the commit that raised the pin to it
# with the Gate stage. The release named here must
# read this commit's gate.toml, which refuses keys it does not know.
